placement=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$body_file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" '\\\\\\\\n130-        BEGIN {\\\\\\\\n131-            while ((getline line < replacement) > 0) {\\\\\\\\n132-                body = body (body == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" ? \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" : \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") line\\\\\\\\n133-            }\\\\\\\\n134-            close(replacement)\\\\\\\\n135-        }\\\\\\\\n136-        $0 == heading {\\\\\\\\n137-            if (found++) exit 2\\\\\\\\n138-            print\\\\\\\\n139-            print \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n140-            print body\\\\\\\\n141-            skipping = 1\\\\\\\\n142-            next\\\\\\\\n143-        }\\\\\\\\n144-        skipping && /^## / { skipping = 0; print \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" }\\\\\\\\n145-        !skipping { print }\\\\\\\\n146-        END { if (found != 1) exit 2 }\\\\\\\\n147-    ' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" > \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$temporary_file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" || plan_die \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Section heading was not found exactly once: $heading\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n148-    mv \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$temporary_file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n149-    trap - RETURN\\\\\\\\n150-}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_40\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"agent_message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I’m replacing the generated placeholders with executable instructions and handoffs. The key planning decision is explicit: the fourth generated button is the fourth appended button, not the initial button.\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_41\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'PLANNING_SKILL_DIR=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T081559Z-pilot-142-iterative-131-clean/1.3.1/worker/planning\\\\\\\\nPLAN=basic-test-proof-1.3.1-20260811T081559Z-pilot-142-iterative-131-clean-isolated-plan\\\\\\\\nU=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No prior implementation goal exists. The future executor starts from the benchmark request and must create button-chain.html as a new single file; this proof did not create or inspect any HTML.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The requested behavior depends on a precise relationship between DOM structure, completion styling, last-button click logic, and finish rendering. Separating those targets prevents an executor from hiding extra behavior inside a broad implementation step.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract scope -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"This goal covers only future edits to button-chain.html for the named DOM subtree, style selector, click handler, and completion renderer. It excludes browser execution, automated test creation, framework installation, server setup, and any file outside button-chain.html.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract affected-areas -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Future affected areas are button-chain.html #button-chain-app, button-chain.html .completion-message, button-chain.html handleButtonClick(event), and button-chain.html renderFinishedState(). No data store, backend, routing, asset pipeline, or external service is affected.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"W01 has no implementation dependency. W02 depends on the completion element contract from W01. W03 depends on W01. W04 depends on W02 and W03. The downstream handoff to W05 is a complete local HTML file ready for browser clicks.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Use a generated-button count stored in the page script, append only when event.target is the current last button, and call renderFinishedState() instead of appending when that current last button represents generated button 4. Guard the off-by-one case by naming generated buttons distinctly from the initial button in code or state.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract goal-size-exception -p 10.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Not applicable. This goal owns four mutually necessary implementation work units, within the 2 to 10 work-unit limit.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"This goal starts after W01 through W04 are implemented. The required handoff is an implemented button-chain.html local file with one initial button, generated-button append logic, completion styling, and finished-state rendering.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The future task is a UI interaction, so source inspection alone cannot prove that direct clicks append exactly one button or that the final visible border is present. US-01 is the acceptance contract for the user-visible flow.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification scope -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"This goal covers only the bounded browser flow in US-01 and its evidence. It excludes modifying button-chain.html during verification, using console or storage shortcuts, weakening the story, or marking it passed without direct click evidence.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification affected-areas -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The verification target is the rendered local button-chain.html page in a browser. Plan artifacts affected during execution are ui-user-stories.md, ui-story-runs/US-01.md, bugs.md if failures are found, and the goal progress tracker.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"W05 depends on W01, W02, W03, and W04. Its handoff is recorded browser evidence for US-01, including whether the exact text finished is visible with a white border and whether any bug register entries were opened or resolved.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Run the cached direct-click sequence exactly as written after the future HTML exists. If any click adds more than one button, responds from a non-last button, fails to clear the document, uses non-lowercase text, or lacks a visible white border, record a bug before changing implementation scope.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification goal-size-exception -p 10.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allowed exception: this goal owns one verification work unit, W05, which is a standalone bounded browser flow permitted by the tagged planning skill goal-size rule.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_41\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'PLANNING_SKILL_DIR=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T081559Z-pilot-142-iterative-131-clean/1.3.1/worker/planning\\\\\\\\nPLAN=basic-test-proof-1.3.1-20260811T081559Z-pilot-142-iterative-131-clean-isolated-plan\\\\\\\\nU=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No prior implementation goal exists. The future executor starts from the benchmark request and must create button-chain.html as a new single file; this proof did not create or inspect any HTML.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The requested behavior depends on a precise relationship between DOM structure, completion styling, last-button click logic, and finish rendering. Separating those targets prevents an executor from hiding extra behavior inside a broad implementation step.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract scope -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"This goal covers only future edits to button-chain.html for the named DOM subtree, style selector, click handler, and completion renderer. It excludes browser execution, automated test creation, framework installation, server setup, and any file outside button-chain.html.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract affected-areas -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Future affected areas are button-chain.html #button-chain-app, button-chain.html .completion-message, button-chain.html handleButtonClick(event), and button-chain.html renderFinishedState(). No data store, backend, routing, asset pipeline, or external service is affected.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"W01 has no implementation dependency. W02 depends on the completion element contract from W01. W03 depends on W01. W04 depends on W02 and W03. The downstream handoff to W05 is a complete local HTML file ready for browser clicks.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Use a generated-button count stored in the page script, append only when event.target is the current last button, and call renderFinishedState() instead of appending when that current last button represents generated button 4. Guard the off-by-one case by naming generated buttons distinctly from the initial button in code or state.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:01-button-chain-contract goal-size-exception -p 10.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Not applicable. This goal owns four mutually necessary implementation work units, within the 2 to 10 work-unit limit.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"This goal starts after W01 through W04 are implemented. The required handoff is an implemented button-chain.html local file with one initial button, generated-button append logic, completion styling, and finished-state rendering.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The future task is a UI interaction, so source inspection alone cannot prove that direct clicks append exactly one button or that the final visible border is present. US-01 is the acceptance contract for the user-visible flow.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification scope -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"This goal covers only the bounded browser flow in US-01 and its evidence. It excludes modifying button-chain.html during verification, using console or storage shortcuts, weakening the story, or marking it passed without direct click evidence.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification affected-areas -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The verification target is the rendered local button-chain.html page in a browser. Plan artifacts affected during execution are ui-user-stories.md, ui-story-runs/US-01.md, bugs.md if failures are found, and the goal progress tracker.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"W05 depends on W01, W02, W03, and W04. Its handoff is recorded browser evidence for US-01, including whether the exact text finished is visible with a white border and whether any bug register entries were opened or resolved.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Run the cached direct-click sequence exactly as written after the future HTML exists. If any click adds more than one button, responds from a non-last button, fails to clear the document, uses non-lowercase text, or lacks a visible white border, record a bug before changing implementation scope.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" goal:02-ui-story-verification goal-size-exception -p 10.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allowed exception: this goal owns one verification work unit, W05, which is a standalone bounded browser flow permitted by the tagged planning skill goal-size rule.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Updated section\\\\\\\\nUpdated section\\\\\\\\nUpdated section\\\\\\\\nUpdated section\\\\\\\\nUpdated section\\\\\\\\nUpdated section\\\\\\\\nUpdated section\\\\\\\\nUpdated section\\\\\\\\nUpdated section\\\\\\\\nUpdated section\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_42\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"agent_message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The goals now describe their scope, dependencies, risks, and handoffs. I’m filling each atomic step with direct future-execution instructions and acceptance criteria tied to its single work unit.\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_43\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'PLANNING_SKILL_DIR=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T081559Z-pilot-142-iterative-131-clean/1.3.1/worker/planning\\\\\\\\nPLAN=basic-test-proof-1.3.1-20260811T081559Z-pilot-142-iterative-131-clean-isolated-plan\\\\\\\\nU=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/01-step-initial-markup instructions -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Create button-chain.html with a complete minimal HTML document. Inside the named #button-chain-app subtree, render exactly one initial button at load and no generated buttons. Give the button user-visible text that distinguishes it from generated buttons without using the reserved completion text finished.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/01-step-initial-markup acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A reviewer can identify one #button-chain-app subtree containing exactly one initial button in the initial DOM. No generated-button elements or completion message are present before any click.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/01-step-initial-markup handoff -p 7.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"W02 can rely on a completion-message element being absent initially and W03 can rely on one initial button as the starting current last button.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/02-step-completion-style instructions -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"In button-chain.html, define the .completion-message selector so the final message has a visible white border. Keep this work unit limited to presentation for the completion message and do not add click behavior here.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/02-step-completion-style acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The .completion-message selector includes a white border value that is visible against the chosen page background, with enough padding or spacing for the border to be seen around the finished text.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/02-step-completion-style handoff -p 7.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"W04 can use class completion-message when rendering the final state.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/03-step-last-button-click instructions -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"In handleButtonClick(event), determine whether the clicked button is the current last button in the chain. If it is not the current last button, do not append a button. If it is the current last button and fewer than four generated buttons exist, append exactly one new generated button below it and update the generated-button count.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/03-step-last-button-click acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Each valid click before completion adds one and only one button after the previous last button. Clicking an older button does not add another button. The initial button is not counted as a generated button.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/03-step-last-button-click handoff -p 7.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"W04 can rely on an accurate generated-button count and last-button detection when deciding whether the fourth generated button was pressed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/04-step-finished-state instructions -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"In renderFinishedState(), clear the document body or the complete app root so prior buttons are removed. Render only the exact lowercase text finished in an element using .completion-message when handleButtonClick(event) receives a click on the fourth generated button.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/04-step-finished-state acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"After the fourth generated button is pressed, no buttons remain, the visible text is exactly finished in lowercase, and the message uses the visible white-border styling from W02.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/04-step-finished-state handoff -p 7.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"W05 can verify the full path by clicking the initial button and then generated buttons 1 through 4, expecting completion only after generated button 4.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:02-ui-story-verification/01-step-ui-story-us-01 objective -p 4.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Verify US-01 with direct browser clicks after the future implementation exists.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:02-ui-story-verification/01-step-ui-story-us-01 instructions -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Open the implemented button-chain.html as a local file in a browser. Follow ui-story-runs/US-01.md exactly: click the current last button five times total, starting with the initial button and ending with generated button 4. Record the URL, decisive screenshot or observation, elapsed waits, and pass or bug status in the story artifacts.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:02-ui-story-verification/01-step-ui-story-us-01 acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"US-01 is passed only when direct clicks show exactly one new button after each pre-completion click and the final click clears the document to exactly finished with a visible white border. Any deviation is entered in bugs.md before implementation fixes are planned.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:02-ui-story-verification/01-step-ui-story-us-01 handoff -p 7.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The initiative can be marked complete only after US-01 evidence is recorded as passed and bugs.md contains no unresolved entries.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_43\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'PLANNING_SKILL_DIR=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T081559Z-pilot-142-iterative-131-clean/1.3.1/worker/planning\\\\\\\\nPLAN=basic-test-proof-1.3.1-20260811T081559Z-pilot-142-iterative-131-clean-isolated-plan\\\\\\\\nU=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/01-step-initial-markup instructions -p 5.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Create button-chain.html with a complete minimal HTML document. Inside the named #button-chain-app subtree, render exactly one initial button at load and no generated buttons. Give the button user-visible text that distinguishes it from generated buttons without using the reserved completion text finished.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" section \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PLAN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" step:01-button-chain-contract/01-step-initial-markup acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A reviewer can identify one #button-chain-app subtree containing exactly one initial button in the initial DOM. No generated-button elements or completion message are present before any click.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$U\\\\\\\\\\\\\